  "text": {
    "tagline": "Sounds from the deep ocean.",
    "blurb": "Underwater listening stations hear the ocean as nobody else can: the slow upsweep, ice cracking off a shelf, whales a basin away, ship screws, the deepest trench. {count} presets turn those recordings into drones, textures and deep effects.",
    "intro": [
      "Listening Post, Data Volume 7, collects {count} presets made from long-range hydrophone recordings of the Pacific. The sounds were sped up or slowed from frequencies too low or too high to hear, as the original researchers did to listen to them.",
      "Each preset is named for its source event. The manual lists what each recording is, where it was made and how it was changed."
    ],
    "maker_note": [
      "We resell public scientific data on disc for schools, libraries and the curious. This is the first volume we have made for musicians.",
